target/
**/*.rs.bk
*.pending-snap
.DS_Store
.claude/worktrees/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# cargo-mutants run output (regenerated every run; the reviewed artifact is
# the accepted-survivors list, not this directory).
mutants.out/
mutants.out.old/

# `verify` writes into the crate under test (a known gap in TODO.md), so a
# run inside demos/ leaves these behind. Neither belongs in the repository:
# `ply.lock` is a record of a run, and committing one invites a later run to
# reuse a recorded verdict instead of earning it -- the whole point of this
# demo is a run that earned something. The generated harness module is
# rewritten on every verify. Dropped once already in 881e872; ignored here so
# it stops being an easy mistake. Real projects DO commit ply.lock (D14) --
# this is scoped to the demo on purpose.
demos/verified-green/ply.lock
demos/verified-green/src/ply_generated.rs

# Same reasoning, and the one that bites hardest: `crates/ply-core/ply.yaml` is
# Ply's document about Ply's own library, so a lock committed from a developer's
# machine is exactly the stale green this project exists to prevent. CI earns
# its verdicts. (D14 still holds for real downstream projects -- they should
# commit theirs.)
crates/ply-core/ply.lock
crates/ply-cli/ply.lock

# The evidence record Ply writes about *itself* when the self-check is run
# by hand (`cargo ply verify crates/ply-core`). Anchored to the product
# crates on purpose: a `ply.lock` under `tests/fixtures/` is a deliberate
# test input and stays tracked.
#
# The-Ply-Spec.md D14 says a project's `ply.lock` is committed, and for a
# project using Ply that is right -- it is what stops CI re-proving what is
# already proven. This repository is the exception for the same reason its
# evidence page is published only from CI: a record committed from a
# contributor's machine would let CI reuse results earned on hardware,
# toolchains and engine versions nobody reviewing the pull request can see.
# Ply's evidence about Ply has to be earned by the run that reports it.
/crates/*/ply.lock
